  Part 2 — Do this ONCE on the Pi (sets up the automation)

  On your Pi (you can sit at it for this part — it's the only time you need to)

  1. Open a Terminal on the Pi (the black screen icon on the taskbar, or right-click desktop → Open Terminal)
  2. Go to the repo folder:
  cd ~/rf-monitor
  3. Pull the latest code (which includes the new scripts you just pushed):
  git pull
  4. Make the scripts executable (Linux requires this before running a script):
  chmod +x RtlSdrTest/scripts/pi-setup.sh RtlSdrTest/scripts/pi-update.sh
  5. Go into the project folder:
  cd RtlSdrTest
  6. Run the setup (use hackrf or rtlsdr depending on which radio you have plugged in):
  sudo bash scripts/pi-setup.sh hackrf
  6. This will print progress. It builds the project which takes about a minute. At the end you'll see === Done ===.

  That's it. The Pi is now set up. You never need to do Part 2 again unless you wipe the Pi or move the repo.

